  "starterCode": "import torch\n\ndef pytorch_build_simple_nn_from_scratch(x: list, W1: list, b1: list, W2: list, b2: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Simple Neural Network** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch, numpy as np\n\ndef pytorch_build_simple_nn_from_scratch(x: list, W1: list, b1: list, W2: list, b2: list) -> list:\n    h = torch.relu(torch.matmul(torch.tensor(x, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(W1, dtype=torch.float32)) + torch.tensor(b1, dtype=torch.float32))\n    out = torch.matmul(h, torch.tensor(W2, dtype=torch.float32)) + torch.tensor(b2, dtype=torch.float32)\n    return np.round(out.numpy(), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
